       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg daily is well above the maximum labeled dose of 10 mg, and I don't know of a standard indication for it. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk to the patient, and I can't verify the reason behind the dose. Entering it as written could lead to serious harm if it's given.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Change the dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right now.\n- **Get a second check.** If a specialist or protocol really calls for 50 mg, talk to pharmacy or the prescriber first. Once that's done, tell me the rationale and who approved it. I can then enter the order with that in the note, though I'd still want it reviewed by pharmacy.\n- **Use another route.** You can place this order directly through your hospital's override process. That process has the required pharmacist verification.\n\nWhich of these would you like to do?"
      }
